# EduGenesis OS - checkout normalisation (PG-19).
#
# Git must never rewrite a byte that the reproducibility chain hashes. Text
# files are normalised to LF in the repository. A Windows checkout with
# core.autocrlf=true materialises CRLF, so the same content can occupy different
# raw bytes on two machines; that is why the release-approval subject is hashed
# in canonical LF form (tools/approval-subject.mjs) and why tools/verify-repro.mjs
# compares the GENERATED evidence rather than the checkout form. Binary and
# generated files are marked so Git never attempts a text conversion at all.
#
# WHY `-text` on artifacts: the attestation, the checksums manifest and the SBOM
# are compared byte-for-byte by tools/verify-repro.mjs. A newline translation on
# checkout would break a legitimate reproduction without any code changing.

* text=auto

# Source, configuration and documentation: normalised, never converted again.
*.ts   text
*.mts  text
*.js   text
*.mjs  text
*.json text
*.md   text
*.yml  text
*.yaml text
*.css  text
*.html text
*.sql  text
*.ps1  text
*.sh   text

# Evidence and generated output: bytes are evidence; never translate them.
artifacts/** -text
artifacts/checksums.sha256 -text
artifacts/attestation.json -text
artifacts/sbom.cdx.json -text

# Binary payloads.
*.png  binary
*.jpg  binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif  binary
*.ico  binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.pdf  binary
*.sqlite binary
*.sqlite3 binary
*.db   binary
*.zip  binary
*.gz   binary
